# The toolbar's right group with two pinned extensions, as in Arc 1.171 (window capture, 8 Nov 2026):
# 32 pt boxes 4 pt apart, so the icons sit on a 36 pt pitch, centred 129, 93, 57 (sliders) and 21
# (Split View) pt from the card edge. Cra drew 34 pt boxes edge to edge, Split View 23 pt in.
# The developer bar has Extensions, the pins, then Split View as 28 pt boxes edge to edge, 5 pt in.
# A focused split pane ends in options and close (32 pt, edge to edge, close centred 21 pt in), the
# sliders 4 pt before them and the pins on the 36 pt pitch.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
port 47125
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": true}
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/Extension
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/SidePanelExtension
relaunch
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=pins
wait 3
cra://debug?pinExtension=${EXTENSION_ID}
cra://debug?pinExtension=${SIDE_PANEL_EXTENSION_ID}
wait 2
snapshot PaneToolbarView toolbar-pinned-extensions
cra://action/toggleDeveloperMode
wait 2
snapshot PaneToolbarView toolbar-pinned-developer
cra://action/toggleDeveloperMode
wait 1
cra://action/addSplitView
wait 2
cra://action/previousSplitPane
wait 2
snapshot PaneToolbarView,0 toolbar-pinned-split-pane
reject-log fault:
